  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jaredpalmer/kev/zipball/kev-family",
  "body": "The Kev family: **Kev-0.8B**, **Kev-4B**, **Kev-9B** — open decision models, all on Qwen3.5 bases. Typed questions in, calibrated probabilities out, one forward pass, no text generation. Each is a LoRA adapter (r=16) plus a pointer head on a frozen Qwen base; the base model downloads on first load.\n\n**2026-09-21 update:** All three models received a short second training pass on generated examples (policy cases with explicit day counts; evidence-free cases trained toward a uniform answer). Locked test, out of domain: Kev-9B 0.837 → **0.852** (+1.8 pp [+0.8, +2.9]), Kev-4B 0.832 → **0.837**, Kev-0.8B 0.668 → **0.684**. The pre-delta weights are attached as `*-v7-base.tar.gz` and on the Hub at revision `v7-base`. Two opt-in serving settings: `KEV_TEMPERATURE=2.0` (calibration) and `KEV_DATE_FACTS=1` (day counts between dates in the state).\n\n**2026-09-20 update:** the family moved to Qwen3.5 bases (same training data and recipe as before). On the locked test, out of domain: Kev-9B 0.837 (Kev-8B was 0.780), Kev-4B 0.832 (was 0.806), Kev-0.8B 0.668 (Kev-0.6B was 0.642), with lower Brier scores. They need `transformers >= 5.17`, and they are slower on Apple Silicon (no fast DeltaNet kernels on MPS; ~0.8 s per five-question request for the 4B vs 0.17 s for the Qwen3 one). The previous Qwen3 checkpoints are attached as `kev-0.6b-qwen3.tar.gz`, `kev-4b-qwen3.tar.gz` and `kev-8b-qwen3.tar.gz`, remain on the Hub (`jaredpalmer/kev-0.6b`, `jaredpalmer/kev-4b@qwen3`, `jaredpalmer/kev-8b`), and are no longer developed.\n\nSame weights as on the Hub ([collection](https://huggingface.co/collections/jaredpalmer/kev-6aad9d0ea49f2589665e07cd)). Each tarball contains the adapter, `head.pt`, tokenizer files, the model card, the trial's `result.json` and `provenance.json`, and the locked-test read (`locked_test.json`).\n\n| | base | in-distribution (dev / locked test) | out-of-domain (dev / locked test) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Kev-9B | Qwen3.5-9B-Base | 0.872 / 0.874 | 0.822 / 0.852 |\n| Kev-4B | Qwen3.5-4B-Base | 0.872 / 0.871 | 0.797 / 0.837 |\n| Kev-0.8B | Qwen3.5-0.8B-Base | 0.825 / 0.834 | 0.652 / 0.684 |\n| Kev-8B (Qwen3) | Qwen3-8B-Base | 0.863 / 0.870 | 0.796 / 0.780 |\n| Kev-4B (Qwen3) | Qwen3-4B-Base | 0.854 / 0.856 | 0.790 / 0.806 |\n| Kev-0.6B (Qwen3) | Qwen3-0.6B-Base | 0.801 / 0.808 | 0.620 / 0.642 |\n| Jev (hosted reference) | – | 0.845 / – | 0.857 / – |\n\nSame frozen items for every row. **Start with Kev-4B.**\n\n```bash\ntar -xzf kev-4b.tar.gz\nKEV_DTYPE=bf16 uv run --extra serve python -m kev.serve --run kev-4b --port 8009\n```\n\nVerify: `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS.txt`. Model cards with per-source numbers, limits and recipes: `docs/model-cards/`. The Qwen3.5 experiment and its pre-registered criteria: `PLAN_Qwen35.md`. Research log: `PLAN.md`.\n\nThe 0.5B prototype remains at [v0.1.0](https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev/releases/tag/v0.1.0).\n"
}
